<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: ["sum", "vector", "composition"],
}
-->

<statement>
	<p>
		Given one number of an amicable pair, compute the other number in the pair. If the given number does not correspond to an amicable pair, return <pf>-1</pf>.
	</p>

	<p>
		Two numbers, <m>M</m> and <m>N</m>, are <em>amicable</em> if the sum of the proper divisors of <m>M</m> is <m>N</m> and the sum of the proper divisors of <m>N</m> is <m>M</m>.
	</p>

	<p>
		For example, 220 and 284 are amicable because the proper divisors of 220 sum to 284, and the proper divisors of 284 sum to 220.
	</p>

	<tabular valign="top" halign="right" top="minor">
		<col width="12%"/>
		<col width="88%" halign="left"/>
		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell>Inputs:</cell>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>num</pf> (1 x 1) integer</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell>Outputs:</cell>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>other</pf> (1 x 1) the amicable partner of <pf>num</pf>, or <pf>-1</pf> if none exists.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row>
			<cell>Details:</cell>
			<cell>
				<p>Implement this by <em>calling</em> your <pf>HW2P1_vector_sum</pf> and <pf>HW2P2_proper_divisors</pf> functions.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p>Do not use a <pf>for</pf> or <pf>while</pf> loop in this function.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
	</tabular>

	<p>
	Examples:
	<program>
		<code>
			friend = is_amicable(983)
			% should return
			% friend = -1
		</code>
	</program>
	<program>
		<code>
			friend = is_amicable(18416)
			% should return
			% friend = 17296
		</code>
	</program>
	</p>
</statement>
